  "markdown": "![](https://www.eda.europa.eu/images/default-source/header-background/bgr-procurement.jpg)\n\n# Procurement\n\nEconomic operators interested in participating in the procurement procedures launched by the European Defence Agency for the supply of goods and/or services can find the necessary information here below.\n\n![procurement-image](https://www.eda.europa.eu/images/default-source/header-background/procurement-image.jpg)\n\n## Ongoing Calls For Tenders\n\nEDA/2026/OP/0010\n\n### Service Framework Contract for the provision of “Nuclear Technologies for EU Defence Energy Systems (NUCLEUS) ...\n\nPublication date: 12 Oct 2026\n\nDeadline: 16 November 2026\n\nEDA/2026/OP/0009\n\n### Media and Communication Support Services\n\nPublication date: 31 August 2026\n\nDeadline: 12 October 2026\n\nEDA/2026/OP/0007\n\n### Provision of energy supplies (electricity and gas) to EDA's premises\n\nPublication date: 13 August 2026\n\nDeadline: 17 September 2026\n\n**[All Closed EDA Tenders on EU & Funding Tenders Portal](https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/opportunities/calls-for-tenders?isExactMatch=true&status=31094503&order=DESC&pageNumber=1&pageSize=50&sortBy=startDate&cftPartyLegalEntityId=47352396)**\n\nCollaborative procurement at EDA\n\n## What is collaborative procurement at EDA?\n\nCollaborative procurement at EDA refers to situations where two or more participating Member States harmonise requirements and aggregate demand in order to carry out a procurement together, typically under an EDA ad hoc programme or project.\n\nEDA may support such initiatives by:\n\n- Assisting in the preparation of the procurement.\n- Conducting procurement procedures on behalf of participating Member States.\n- Establishing framework arrangements or contracts enabling Member States to place orders.\n\nIn these cases, EDA typically does not procure for its own needs but acts on behalf of participating Member States.\n\n## Which rules apply?\n\nProcurement may follow the EDA financial rules (Council Decision 2016/1353), which are similar to those applicable to EU institutions and agencies.\n\nAlternatively, collaborative procurement at EDA may be conducted under:\n\n- Directive 2009/81/EC on Defence and Security Procurement.\n- Ad hoc legal and procedural frameworks.\n- Programme-specific rules agreed by participating Member States.\n\nThe applicable framework determines eligibility and participation conditions.\n\n## Who can participate?\n\nParticipation depends on the applicable rules, but economic operators should note the following principles:\n\n- Access is primarily open to operators established in the EU and EEA.\n- Access may be restricted depending on Member States' decisions.\n- Third-country participation may be allowed under specific conditions.\n- Participation through consortia or subcontracting may be possible.\n- Additional defence-specific requirements may apply.\n\n## How are opportunities published?\n\nOpportunities under collaborative procurement at EDA may be published through:\n\n- TED – Tenders Electronic Daily.\n- The EDA procurement webpage.\n- Market consultation and industry engagement activities.\n\nGiven the specific nature of defence procurement, some preparatory activities or documentation may not be publicly available.\n\n## How can economic operators engage?\n\nEconomic operators interested in participating in collaborative procurement at EDA are encouraged to:\n\n- Regularly monitor EDA's procurement-related publicity webpage.\n- Consult EDA's EU Funding, SME Corner and B2B Platform webpages.\n- Participate in market consultations and industry events.\n- Ensure compliance with eligibility and security requirements.\n- Align capabilities with collaborative defence initiatives.\n\nFor further information, economic operators may contact EDA at\n**JP@eda.europa.eu**.\n\nDue to the high volume of correspondence received, EDA may not be able to respond to unsolicited enquiries.\n\n## Other notices\n\n[**Ex-ante publicity notice for the negotiated procedure ref.26.CSD-INF.NP3.379“...**\\\\\n\\\\\nStarted: 25 August 2026\\\\\n\\\\\nClosing: 15 September 2026](https://www.eda.europa.eu/procurement/other-notices/ex-ante-publicity-notice-for-the-negotiated-procedure-ref.26.csd-inf.np3.379-collection-of-waste-from-eda-premises)\n\n[**Ex-ante publicity notice for the negotiated procedure CF SEDSS IV 26.RTI.NP3....**\\\\\n\\\\\nStarted: 17 July 2026\\\\\n\\\\\nClosing: 04 August 2026](https://www.eda.europa.eu/procurement/other-notices/ex-ante-publicity-notice-for-the-negotiated-procedure-cf-sedss-iv-26.rti.np3.108-for--accommodation-and-catering-procurement-for-cf-sedss-iv-table-top-exercise-(ttx))\n\n[**Annual List of Contractors 2025**](https://www.eda.europa.eu/procurement/other-notices/annual-list-of-contractors-2025)\n\n[**Call for Expression of Interest: ref. No 24.CSD.NP3.452 - List of Vendors for...**\\\\\n\\\\\nStarted: 01 April 2025\\\\\n\\\\\nClosing: 31 December 2028](https://www.eda.europa.eu/procurement/other-notices/ex-ante-publicity-notice-ref.-no-24.csd.np3.452---list-of-vendors-for-the-provision-of-catering-services-for-eda)\n\n## Legal Basis and other related documents\n\n- [EDA Privacy Statement - Azure Active Directory - EDA- DPO-73](https://www.eda.europa.eu/docs/default-source/documents/dpo-privacy-statements/eda-privacy-statement---azure-active-directory---eda--dpo-73.pdf)\n- [General Conditions for Low Value Contracts](https://www.eda.europa.eu/docs/default-source/Defence-Procurement-Gateway/general-conditions-for-low-value-contracts.pdf)\n- [Quick e-Submission Guide for Economic Operators Applicable for Call for Tenders published](https://www.eda.europa.eu/docs/default-source/procurement-library/quick-e-submission-guide-for-economic-operators-applicable-for-call-for-tenders-published.pdf)\n\nOur website uses cookies to improve your user experience. Learn more about our Cookies Policy [here.](https://www.eda.europa.eu/cookies-policy)\n\n[I accept cookies](https://www.eda.europa.eu/procurement#) [I refuse cookies](https://www.eda.europa.eu/procurement#)",
