n/opportunities/calls-for-tenders?isExactMatch=true&amp;status=31094503&amp;order=DESC&amp;pageNumber=1&amp;pageSize=50&amp;sortBy=startDate&amp;cftPartyLegalEntityId=47352396\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"lnk-ext\"><span class=\"label-ext\">All Closed EDA Tenders on EU &amp; Funding Tenders Portal</span><sup class=\"char-ext\"></sup></a>&nbsp;</strong>\n</p>\n\n</div>\n            \n        </div>\n    </div>\n</div><div class=\"sf_cols eda-section latest-sctn\">\n    <div class=\"sf_colsOut sf_1col_1_100\" style=\"\">\n        <div id=\"Main_C040_Col00\" class=\"sf_colsIn sf_1col_1in_100\"><div class=\"sf_cols  latest-sctn-title wdg-container\">\n    <div class=\"sf_colsOut sf_2cols_1_50 title-sctn\" style=\"width: 50%;\">\n        <div id=\"Main_C044_Col00\" class=\"sf_colsIn sf_2cols_1in_50\"><div class=\"sfContentBlock\"><!--\n<h2>Invitation to Bid</h2>-->\n\n</div>\n            \n        </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"sf_colsOut sf_2cols_2_50\" style=\"width: 50%;\">\n        <div id=\"Main_C044_Col01\" class=\"sf_colsIn sf_2cols_2in_50\">            \n        </div>\n    </div>\n</div><div class=\"sfContentBlock\"><div style=\"max-width:1200px;margin:24px auto;padding:0 16px 40px;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;\">\n<details>\n<summary style=\"cursor:pointer;padding:12px 14px;background:#f1f4f7;font-size:26px;\">\nCollaborative procurement at EDA\n</summary>\n<div style=\"padding:15px 0;\">\n<!-- Card 1 -->\n<div style=\"background:#fafafa;border:1px solid #e7e7e7;border-radius:8px;padding:20px;margin-bottom:20px;\">\n<h2 style=\"margin-top:0;color:#0a58ca;\">What is collaborative procurement at EDA?</h2>\n<p>\nCollaborative procurement at EDA refers to situations where two or more participating Member States harmonise requirements and aggregate demand in order to carry out a procurement together, typically under an EDA ad hoc programme or project.\n</p>\n<p>EDA may support such initiatives by:</p>\n<ul style=\"padding-left:20px;line-height:1.6;\">\n    <li>Assisting in the preparation of the procurement.</li>\n    <li>Conducting procurement procedures on behalf of participating Member States.</li>\n    <li>Establishing framework arrangements or contracts enabling Member States to place orders.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>\nIn these cases, EDA typically does not procure for its own needs but acts on behalf of participating Member States.\n</p>\n</div>\n<!-- Card 2 -->\n<div style=\"background:#fafafa;border:1px solid #e7e7e7;border-radius:8px;padding:20px;margin-bottom:20px;\">\n<h2 style=\"margin-top:0;color:#0a58ca;\">Which rules apply?</h2>\n<p>\nProcurement may follow the EDA financial rules (Council Decision 2016/1353), which are similar to those applicable to EU institutions and agencies.\n</p>\n<p>\nAlternatively, collaborative procurement at EDA may be conducted under:\n</p>\n<ul style=\"padding-left:20px;line-height:1.6;\">\n    <li>Directive 2009/81/EC on Defence and Security Procurement.</li>\n    <li>Ad hoc legal and procedural frameworks.</li>\n    <li>Programme-specific rules agreed by participating Member States.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>\nThe applicable framework determines eligibility and participation conditions.\n</p>\n</div>\n<!-- Card 3 -->\n<div style=\"background:#fafafa;border:1px solid #e7e7e7;border-radius:8px;padding:20px;margin-bottom:20px;\">\n<h2 style=\"margin-top:0;color:#0a58ca;\">Who can participate?</h2>\n<p>\nParticipation depends on the applicable rules, but economic operators should note the following principles:\n</p>\n<ul style=\"padding-left:20px;line-height:1.6;\">\n    <li>Access is primarily open to operators established in the EU and EEA.</li>\n    <li>Access may be restricted depending on Member States' decisions.</li>\n    <li>Third-country participation may be allowed under specific conditions.</li>\n    <li>Participation through consortia or subcontracting may be possible.</li>\n    <li>Additional defence-specific requirements may apply.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n<!-- Card 4 -->\n<div style=\"background:#fafafa;border:1px solid #e7e7e7;border-radius:8px;padding:20px;margin-bottom:20px;\">\n<h2 style=\"margin-top:0;color:#0a58ca;\">How are opportunities published?</h2>\n<p>\nOpportunities under collaborative procurement at EDA may be published through:\n</p>\n<ul style=\"padding-left:20px;line-height:1.6;\">\n    <li>TED – Tenders Electronic Daily.</li>\n    <li>The EDA procurement webpage.</li>\n    <li>Market consultation and industry engagement activities.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>\nGiven the specific nature of defence procurement, some preparatory activities or documentation may not be publicly available.\n</p>\n</div>\n<!-- Card 5 -->\n<div style=\"background:#fafafa;border:1px solid #e7e7e7;border-radius:8px;padding:20px;\">\n<h2 style=\"margin-top:0;color:#0a58ca;\">How can economic operators engage?</h2>\n<p>\nEconomic operators interested in participating in collaborative procurement at EDA are encouraged to:\n</p>\n<ul style=\"padding-left:20px;line-height:1.6;\">\n    <li>Regularly monitor EDA's procurement-related publicity webpage.</li>\n    <li>Consult EDA's EU Funding, SME Corner and B2B Platform webpages.</li>\n    <li>Participate in market consultations and industry events.</li>\n    <li>Ensure compliance with eligibility and security requirements.</li>\n    <li>Align capabilities with collaborative defence initiatives.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>\nFor further information, economic operators may contact EDA at\n<strong>JP@eda.europa.eu</strong>.\n</p>\n<p>\nDue to the high volume of correspondence received, EDA may not be able to respond to unsolicited enquiries.\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n</details>\n</div>\n\n</div><div>\n\t\n\n<div class=\"latest-sctn-title wdg-container\">\n    <div class=\"title-sctn\">\n         <h2></h2>\n    </div>\n</div>\n  \n\n       <section class=\"LatestProcurement\">\n             <div id=\"LatestContent\" class=\"latest-content sctn-content wdg-container\">\n\t            <div class=\"wdg-row\">\n\t            \n\t\t    </div>\n\t  